                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "DO NOT BUY - Completely unplayable on modern systems (Permanent Black Screen on startup)\n\nF.E.A.R. 1 runs completely fine. F.E.A.R. 3 works right out of the box. But F.E.A.R. 2 is an absolute technical disaster on modern Windows.\n\nThe game crashes into a permanent black screen right upon launch. I have tried every single community fix available:\n\nEditing settings.cfg (toggling fullscreen, lowering resolution to 720p, forcing 60Hz, disabling Vsync).\n\nForcing launch commands via Steam options (-windowed, -width, -height).\n\nDropping wrappers into the directory (DXVK, dinput8 hooks, DirectInput fixes).\n\nChanging audio sample rates to 16-bit/24-bit 48kHz and adjusting DPI/compatibility settings.\n\nDisconnecting USB peripherals and gamepads.\n\nAbsolutely nothing works. Monolith and Warner Bros. have completely abandoned this title, leaving a broken port for sale on the store that refuses to initialize modern Direct3D 9 / display pipelines.\n\nSave your money and your time. Do not buy this garbage port unless you keep a vintage Windows XP rig lying around.",
